<title>JAPAN: Yaohan shares up sharply after sell-off.</title>
<headline>Yaohan shares up sharply after sell-off.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Yaohan Japan Corp, a regional supermarket chain operator, had jumped sharply by early Monday afternoon.</p>
<p>Brokers said the shares had been oversold after dropping sharply on market speculation about the company's future earnings.</p>
<p>As of 0410 GMT, the share was up 74 yen at 574 yen, making it the largest percentage gainer on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange. Volume was 949,000 shares.</p>
</text>
